Follow-up to #10172 (ULTRASTABLE-CLAIMS-1). Live defect:
qnfo.org/platform read "3 of 7 claims pass" because four probes held ";
" inside a detail string, and both the gateway guard and
`remediation_consumer.is_literal_select` refuse any semicolon.

- **Back end:** `migrations/2026-11-10-ultrastable-claims-semicolon.sql`
rewrites those detail strings with ", " in `product_claims` and the
`claim-ultrastable-*` contracts.
- **Front end:** qnfo-gateway 3.64.1 ignores semicolons inside string
literals; a real second statement is still refused (tests for both; the
new case fails on 3.64.0).
- `scripts/product_claims_probe_guard_test.py` runs the consumer's own
guard over every stored probe (fails on the old text), wired into
`product-boundary.test.mjs`.

work-claim: unreachable (proxy 403 to
qnfo-deploy-guard.q08.workers.dev); no other open PR touches these paths
probes: qnfo-gateway/probes.json unchanged (the /platform probe added in
#10172 covers it)

## Verified
pr-checks versions and scans green; platform-claims 13 passed;
product-boundary 5 passed; migration check ok; pre_push_check ok.


